  "generalizations": [
    "The current walk is a schematic sequence and does not encode distances, entrances, pedestrian access, or temporary closures.",
    "Former east and west gate points are approximate historical locators derived from the cited gazetteer; they are not surviving structures.",
    "The Han panel intentionally avoids an ancient-city polygon because early Jincheng County locations and movements remain disputed.",
    "The later old-city core is an editorial reading area, not a surveyed wall reconstruction or a claim of continuous occupation from the Han period.",
    "West and east expansion arrows summarize railway, industrial, and planning history; they are not administrative boundaries or a complete industrial map."
